  <article class="article">
    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rental Cost</span>
    <h1>Honda Air Blade Rental Price in Hanoi</h1>
    <p>The Honda Air Blade is the largest automatic scooter in our published rental list and the machine many riders picture when they imagine a Vietnamese city scooter: sharp styling, a long seat and a confident stance in traffic. This guide covers the verified Honda Air Blade rental price in Hanoi for every rental period, how it compares with the Honda Vision it shares a price tier with, and who the Air Blade genuinely suits.</p>
    <p>Every figure below matches our published <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, the complete source of verified fleet prices. Nothing here is an estimate or a promotion.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">What the Air Blade is like to ride</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Honda Air Blade rental prices in Hanoi</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">How daily, weekly and monthly rates compare</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Air Blade versus Honda Vision</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Air Blade versus the budget tier</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-6">Who should rent the Air Blade</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-7">How to book an Air Blade</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="sec-1">What the Air Blade is like to ride</h2>
    <p>The Air Blade is a fully automatic scooter, so riding it is twist-and-go. What separates it from smaller automatics is presence: the body is longer, the seat is roomy enough for a rider and passenger without feeling packed, and the riding position is relaxed for taller riders who feel folded onto compact scooters.</p>
    <p>In traffic, that size is a double-edged sword in the way all larger scooters are. The Air Blade is steady and comfortable when the road opens up, and it takes Hanoi's frequent restarts without fuss. In the narrowest Old Quarter lanes, riders simply go slower, which is what everyone does regardless of bike. If you are weighing whether a bigger scooter is harder to park, the honest answer is slightly yes, and the practical answer is that thousands of locals park larger scooters in this city every day. Our <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> guide covers riding and parking in the densest part of the city.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-2">Honda Air Blade rental prices in Hanoi</h2>
    <p>The verified Honda Air Blade rental price in Hanoi is 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week, and 1,500,000 VND per month. Unlike the Vision's monthly range, the Air Blade has a single verified monthly figure of 1,500,000 VND.</p>
    <p>These rates sit in the premium automatic tier, alongside the Honda Vision. You can verify every number against the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">full rental price list</a> before you arrive, and the rate you are quoted at the shop is the published rate for the period you choose.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-3">How daily, weekly and monthly rates compare</h2>
    <p>Seven daily rentals of an Air Blade would cost 1,400,000 VND against the 1,000,000 VND weekly rate, a saving of 400,000 VND. Over a month the gap widens sharply: thirty daily rentals would cost 6,000,000 VND, while the monthly rate is a flat 1,500,000 VND, roughly a quarter of the stacked daily price.</p>
    <p>Per day, the weekly rate works out to about 143,000 VND and the monthly rate to 50,000 VND. The Air Blade's monthly figure is also lower than the Vision's monthly range of 1,800,000&ndash;2,000,000 VND, which surprises renters who compare only the identical daily rates. For long stays, that monthly difference matters; the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental in Hanoi</a> hub explains how long-term hire works.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-4">Air Blade versus Honda Vision</h2>
    <p>The Vision and Air Blade rent for the same 200,000 VND per day and 1,000,000 VND per week, but their monthly rates differ: the Air Blade is a flat 1,500,000 VND while the Vision ranges from 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND. For rentals of a month or longer, the Air Blade is the cheaper premium automatic in the published list.</p>
    <p>In character, the Vision is the lighter, simpler city scooter, while the Air Blade is the sportier, larger machine. Riders who prioritize low weight and easy parking tend toward the Vision; riders who want presence, seat space and a more planted feel at speed tend toward the Air Blade. There is no safety difference between them. If you want the Vision's numbers side by side, read the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/honda-vision-rental-price-hanoi/">Honda Vision rental price</a> guide.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-5">Air Blade versus the budget tier</h2>
    <p>The budget tier rents for 150,000 VND per day: the semi-automatic Honda Wave and Yamaha Sirius, and the automatic Honda Click and Yamaha Mio. The Air Blade costs 50,000 VND more per day than any of them, which over a week adds up to a 300,000 VND gap against the weekly rates of 1,000,000 VND versus 700,000 VND.</p>
    <p>Whether that gap is worth paying depends on what you value. The budget automatics are lighter and cheaper; the Air Blade is roomier and more relaxed. For city-only riding on a short stay, plenty of renters are happy with a Click. For longer stays, the monthly figures reverse the feeling of expense: the Air Blade's 1,500,000 VND monthly rate is closer to the budget tier than to its own daily rate. Compare the automatics in the <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/">Hanoi scooter rental</a> hub before deciding.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-6">Who should rent the Air Blade</h2>
    <p>The Air Blade suits riders who want a premium automatic for longer days: commuters crossing districts, riders planning day trips on main paved routes, and taller riders or couples who want more seat. It is also the rational pick among the premium automatics for monthly rentals, given the flat 1,500,000 VND rate.</p>
    <p>It is less necessary for riders whose trips are short, central and low-speed, where a compact automatic does the same job for 50,000 VND less per day. As always, the deciding factor should be sitting on the actual bikes available for your dates. For day trip planning beyond the city, start with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, and for the general rental process read <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/how-to-rent-a-motorbike-in-hanoi/">how to rent a motorbike in Hanoi</a> step by step.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-7">How to book an Air Blade</h2>
    <p>Call <a href="tel:+84942467674">0942 467 674</a>, email <a href="mailto:nguyentuantu8x@gmail.com">nguyentuantu8x@gmail.com</a>, or visit the shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi. We are open 09:00&ndash;21:00 daily, and the rental is completed at the shop. Contact us ahead of your dates so we can confirm an Air Blade is available.</p>
    <p>Know your rental period before you arrive, since the weekly and monthly rates save substantially against daily pricing. For questions about deposits, documents or rental conditions, ask directly and check the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> hub first.</p>

    <h2 id="sec-8">Living with an Air Blade day to day</h2>
    <p>The Air Blade's advantages show up in the unglamorous hours. Crossing the city twice a day, the roomy seat and planted stance make the difference between arriving fresh and arriving folded. On the restart-heavy arterial roads, the automatic transmission does the work the traffic would otherwise dump on your left hand and foot. And on the occasional longer weekend ride, the machine settles into provincial cruising without feeling stretched, which is the main scenario where the premium tier justifies itself.</p>
    <p>Parking is the one place the size asks anything of you. The Air Blade fits everywhere a Vision fits, just with less margin in the tightest rows, and the attendants who run the Old Quarter strips shuffle bikes this size all day without comment. Riders adapt within a day: you simply choose the end-of-row slots when they are available, exactly as locals do on identical machines.</p>
    <p>The financial summary is worth repeating because it is unusual: identical daily and weekly rates with the Vision, but a lower monthly rate, a flat 1,500,000 VND. Short visitors can choose purely on ergonomics; monthly renters should notice they are comparing 1,500,000 VND against 1,800,000&ndash;2,000,000 VND, which is a real difference over a season. Verify both figures on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost hub</a>, and weigh them against the Vision's lighter city manners described in the <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/">scooter hub</a>.</p>

    <p>For riders deciding entirely inside the premium tier, the question is comfort versus budget: the Air Blade's flat 1,500,000 VND monthly rate against the Vision's range, with identical daily and weekly pricing. Sit on both if both are free for your dates, ride the block around the shop before committing, and pick the one that fits your body and your period. The premium tier exists precisely so that choice is worth making; for a week of purely central riding at low speeds, the budget automatics do the same job for 50,000 VND less per day, a comparison worth making honestly before spending more.</p>

    <p>To book, call <a href="tel:+84942467674">0942 467 674</a>, email <a href="mailto:nguyentuantu8x@gmail.com">nguyentuantu8x@gmail.com</a>, or visit the shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi. We are open 09:00&ndash;21:00 daily, and the rental is completed at the shop. Contact us ahead of your dates so we can confirm an Air Blade is available, and mention whether your plan is city riding, longer routes or a full month, because the same bike earns its price differently in each case.</p>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions about Air Blade rental prices</h2>
    <article class="faq-entry">
      <h2>How much does it cost to rent a Honda Air Blade in Hanoi?</h2>
      <p>The verified rates are 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and a flat 1,500,000 VND per month. The Air Blade is the only premium automatic with a single verified monthly figure rather than a range.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-entry">
      <h2>Is the Air Blade cheaper than the Honda Vision for a month?</h2>
      <p>Yes. Both rent for 200,000 VND per day, but the Air Blade's monthly rate is 1,500,000 VND while the Vision's monthly range is 1,800,000&ndash;2,000,000 VND. Over a month the Air Blade is the cheaper premium automatic.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-entry">
      <h2>Is the Air Blade good for two people?</h2>
      <p>It is one of the roomier scooters in the fleet, with a long seat that suits a rider and passenger. As with any bike, ride within your comfort and keep to local traffic norms.</p>
    </article>

